  "failed_attempts_and_corrections": [
    "The initial brace widened the stance by 7.000014 mm while loading the shield. An all-vertex test on the reopened asset detected this in-plane slip despite six valid pad contacts. Held the pad targets fixed throughout brace and regenerated both clean final runs. Final maximum displacement across either LOD is 0.01838 mm, including interpolation between sampled keys.",
    "The first shield-roof probe exposed head vertices above the outer roof by 26.147 mm in brace, 5.931 mm in attack, 13.251 mm in hit and 10.284 mm in death. Lowered the bearing and mask, retracted the head during loading and impact, and reduced the death compression after a prototype drove the jaw 29.012 mm beneath the floor. Every final imported subframe tests the whole head for attachment, checks its triangles against the shield, and raycasts the actual underside above each covered head vertex. Worst final vertical clearances are 14.537 mm at LOD0 and 16.387 mm at LOD1.",
    "The initial matched underside camera cropped the tip of one contact pad. Lowered its aim point and widened the orthographic frame across all three versions, then regenerated the review package."
  ],
